WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
放学下雨，公交刚走，你的鞋也湿了。
It rains after school. You miss the bus and your shoes get wet.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:11.000
等车的时候，有人把伞往你这边挪了一点。
While you wait, someone shifts their umbrella to cover you.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.300
左页记今天的难处，右页记那一小段被照顾。
Put today’s difficulty on the left page and the small kindness on the right.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:22.000
两件事都发生过，可以都留下来。
Both things happened. Both can stay on the page.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.000
写具体一点。“他挪了半把伞，我的书包没再淋湿。”
Be specific. “They moved the umbrella and my bag stayed dry.”

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.000
感恩记录是在练习留意这些本来容易过去的细节。
Gratitude journaling practices noticing details that can slip by.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.200
埃蒙斯和麦卡洛比较过不同记录任务。
Emmons and McCullough compared different journaling assignments.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:44.000
与对照组相比，感恩记录组有些福祉指标更好。
The gratitude groups did better on some well-being measures than control groups.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.000
把这当成可选的小练习。今天找不到也可以空着。
Treat it as an optional exercise. You can leave the page blank today.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.000
刚才的双页写法，是把这个思路用在日常的示范。
The two-page layout is a practical illustration.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:03.000
下次写日记时，给困难和支持各留一个位置。
Next time you journal, give both hardship and support a place.
